# L §6.4 (tally 2.1.6, P29 on T's SR-T1 of #75): a binding's `where` that reads a value decides at run which keys are
# instances, so load can't see that one books before D and refuses nothing. top's where reads from_day: no instance
# before 2026-01-01 exists. 2.1.6's first refcore (522a715) refused topup at load, LOAD-SCENARIO top books on
# 2025-12-30, the where unread. Twin: _where_keys_refused.
=== base.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-02
  start 2025-12-30
  end 2026-01-05

source s "s"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..

place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

input from_day: date

input early: date

ask q: bal(konto, 2026-01-05)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  from_day = 2026-01-01
  early = 2025-01-01
  opening[konto] = 10.00 PLN at 2025-12-30 start
=== scen.tally
scenario topup over hh
  tally 2
  from 2026-01-01

move top[d in days where d >= from_day]: transfers
  on d
  leg cash from world to konto amount 1.00 PLN

ask q_top: bal(konto, 2026-01-05) in topup
=== expect q_top
q_top: 15.00 PLN
  world: topup
  unfulfilled: top[2026-01-01]
  cut 2026-01-02
warning: WARN-UNREAD input early is read by nothing
